---
description: When and how to update Cursor rules as the codebase evolves
globs: "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

- **Add a new rule when:** a pattern appears in 3+ files, reviews repeat the same feedback, or a new library becomes core to the project.
- **Update rules when:** better examples exist in the codebase, edge cases are discovered, or stack versions change.
- **Deprecate rules when:** patterns are removed or replaced — document the migration in the rule.
- **Keep rules DRY:** cross-reference [project-rules.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/project-rules.mdc) and [cursor_rules.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/cursor_rules.mdc) instead of duplicating guidance.
- **Sync with code:** after major refactors, verify rules still match actual folder structure, naming, and dependencies.
